  // ── "How it works" steps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  how
    h1
      title = Browse
      description = Explore the categories and pick a template that matches your project — every one is a complete, working generator.
    h2
      title = Fork
      description = Open it on Perchance, hit save to create your own copy, and start editing main.pjs and the src files — nothing to install.
    h3
      title = Build
      description = Swap in your content, tune the gameplay and style, and publish. Templates ship with demos so there's always something working to start from.

  // ── FAQ accordion ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  faq
    q1
      question = What exactly is a template here?
      answer = Each template is a complete, working Perchance generator you can fork and remix — a starting point that already runs, so you build on top of working code instead of a blank page.
    q2
      question = How do I use one?
      answer = Open any template, click save in the Perchance editor to fork your own copy, then edit the main.pjs lists and src files. Most templates document exactly what to change in their code comments.
    q3
      question = Do the templates work offline or standalone?
      answer = They're regular Perchance generators — they run in any browser and are free to use. Some, like the Boardgame Network and Video Game Network templates, also connect to their network hubs for online play.
    q4
      question = Are the view counts live?
      answer = No — they're snapshots shown in the config for context. They refresh whenever I update the config, or you can edit them yourself.
    q5
      question = Can I submit or request a template?
      answer = This hub is built and maintained by Rathji. Find a template that fits your project and fork it — if you'd like a new one added, get in touch.
    q6
      question = What does the private tag mean?
      answer = A template marked private is shared selectively rather than listed publicly on Perchance — reach out if you need access.

  // ── Footer link columns ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
